e":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.3.stable.steam [77dcf97d8]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable (77dcf97d8) - Windows 10.0.26100 - GLES3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7216) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900KF (32 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe Input.joy_connection_changed signal is not properly emitted, when a Bluetooth controller (Nintendo Switch Pro Controller, DualSense) is disconnected, if there is also an XInput device (Xbox Series) controller connected. It seems, the order in which the controller are connected is important here. If the XInput device has been connected first (or before the Bluetooth devices), Godot will no longer emit the signal, if the Bluetooth device disconnects.\nIf the Bluetooth device connects first or is the only controller, the Input.joy_connection_changed signal will be emitted properly on disconnect\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Have a Nintendo Switch Controller paired via Bluetooth and connect an Xbox controller (or probably any other device, which is handled as XInput device)\n- Start a godot project, which connects with the Input.joy_connection_changed signal and let it print a message, when a controller connects/disconnects\n- Make sure the Xbox controller connects first.\n- Connect the Nintendo Switch Pro Controller (or probably any other Bluetooth controller, which is not handled as XInput)\n- Disconnect the Nintendo Switch Pro controller\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"echelon86","id":199580827,"node_id":"U_kgDOC-Vcmw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199580827?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86","html_url":"https://github.com/echelon86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echelon86/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102942/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}